From: Project Luma <builds@project-luma.local>
Subject: [PATCH] files: ask the portal for the application chooser

The Luma application chooser is a portal backend, so that a sandboxed
application asking OpenURI and a double-click in Files both reach the
same dialog. Files never reached it. Upstream asks the portal only when
it is itself sandboxed, and otherwise builds its own chooser inline, so
the Luma chooser was configured correctly, owned its bus name and
answered activation in 0.2 seconds while ChooseApplication went
uncalled for an entire session.

The portal path taken below is upstream's own, already carrying the
parent window, walking a multiple-file selection and recording recents.
Only the condition that selects it changes.

diff --git a/src/nautilus-files-view.c b/src/nautilus-files-view.c
--- a/src/nautilus-files-view.c
+++ b/src/nautilus-files-view.c
@@ -1497,6 +1497,25 @@
     adw_dialog_close (ADW_DIALOG (dialog));
 }
 
+/* Luma answers application-chooser requests with its own dialog, served over
+ * the AppChooser portal so that every caller gets the same chooser. Upstream
+ * asks the portal only when Files is sandboxed and otherwise builds its own
+ * chooser inline, which is why the Luma chooser could be installed,
+ * configured, activating in 0.2s and still never appear: an unsandboxed Files
+ * never sent the request at all, and ChooseApplication was never called once.
+ *
+ * Widening the condition is all that is needed. The portal path below is
+ * upstream's own and already carries the parent window, walks a
+ * multiple-file selection and records recents, so nothing here is
+ * reimplemented. Set NAUTILUS_LUMA_NATIVE_CHOOSER=1 to get the built-in
+ * dialog back for comparison.
+ */
+static gboolean
+luma_prefers_portal_chooser (void)
+{
+    return g_strcmp0 (g_getenv ("NAUTILUS_LUMA_NATIVE_CHOOSER"), "1") != 0;
+}
+
 static void
 choose_program (NautilusFilesView *view,
                 GList             *files)
@@ -1508,7 +1527,7 @@
 
     parent_window = nautilus_files_view_get_containing_window (view);
 
-    if (nautilus_application_is_sandboxed ())
+    if (luma_prefers_portal_chooser () || nautilus_application_is_sandboxed ())
     {
         sandboxed_choose_program (g_steal_pointer (&files), parent_window);
         return;
